WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.719
wake up, son, wake up,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.720
wake up

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.739
when Christina Lester moved to Palm

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.629
Springs, California, in 2020,

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:22.799
she considered sending her son

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.119
Daniel to the local elementary

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.120
school.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.249
I saw a school across the street

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.659
from my house, so I started to

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.249
think, well, maybe he could go to

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.719
the district school.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.399
But at Julius Corzine Elementary,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.989
the students score well below the

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:36.490
state average in English and math.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.429
There was no way that I was going to

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.049
send my son to a failing school.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.059
So Daniel attends Pome Academy,

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.439
which is part of the Springs Charter

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.519
School Network.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.299
Like all charters.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.619
The school is publicly funded, so

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.689
there's no tuition bill and last

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.009
feels it's well equipped to serve

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.029
Daniel's special needs.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.739
And we leave around

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.419
seven o'clock.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.669
I drive thirty five minutes

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.049
to 40 minutes away

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.379
because it's a charter park academy

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.819
accepts students from as far away as

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:09.929
the next county over.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.249
The problem is it doesn't provide

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.250
transportation.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.969
Having the lack of transportation to

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.589
get our children to school is

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.749
hurting the need for the resources

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.309
for single parents like myself and

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.169
low income families.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.119
We need them the most, but yet we

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.159
still don't have them available.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.569
And this is a nationwide problem

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:29.159
that limits parental choice.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.449
Although it varies by district,

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.099
about two thirds of states don't

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.329
require districts to provide

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:34.649
transportation for charter school

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.249
students.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.389
Like many things in public

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.429
education, the orientation

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.139
that school districts and the public

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.489
sector tends to have toward school

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.379
transportation is that the clients

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.609
of the schools are the school

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.469
districts rather than the clients or

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.089
the parents and what they need.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.979
Andrew Rotherham is a co-founder

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.419
at the nonprofit Bellwether

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.129
Education Partners, which has been

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.749
studying how school transportation

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.099
limits parental choice.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.139
A lot of places it's a struggle

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.969
for parents to get their kids to

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.799
a charter school in suburbs that are

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.329
very car dependent where people may

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.039
have to go great distances, choices

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.359
start to become out of reach.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.979
The one group it was substantial for

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.869
low income minority kids end up

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.069
going the furthest to get to

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:12.899
schools. That's a function of

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.579
parents being in communities where

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.689
they may not have a schooling option

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.519
that they want and having to go go a

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:18.869
great distance to avail themselves

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.129
of one

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.959
K ready to go.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.759
I think in Jesus name.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.659
Amen.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.660
Have a good day.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:29.709
After I dropped him off at

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.049
school, I'll just go to the park.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.879
Typically, I'll spend my whole day

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.279
there in meetings,

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.439
back to back or on phone calls.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.389
I don't have any Wi-Fi

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.169
at the park.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.519
If I have these the bathroom, I'll

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.679
just go to the park

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.939
bathroom.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.979
The longest hours that I've sat

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.899
in the car at the park or is the

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.759
like from 8:30 in the morning to

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:52.760
4:30?

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.929
If Daniel was provided

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.339
with transportation to get to

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.439
school, I could do my work

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:00.549
more efficiently.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.079
Hi, my name is Christina Laster.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.189
I'm the director of policy and

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:04.389
legislation with the National

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.499
Parents Union.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.509
Last year, who spent nearly 13 years

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:08.679
in the San Diego Public School

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.269
System, now works in education

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.679
reform.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.299
There is no funding from the state

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.249
of California that

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.859
is offered to charter schools

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.659
for transportation.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.519
It's not even a line item on

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.289
their budget, like we have a local

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.579
control funding formula.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.469
We have what is called the local

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.179
control and Accountability Plan, and

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.889
there are no resources granted for

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.149
public charter schools.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:32.919
Opponents might say the state

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.539
already has offered parents an

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.799
education that's close to their

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.719
home. That's what zoned neighborhood

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:38.709
schools are.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.119
Why should they be required to

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.379
transport kids to another

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.329
neighborhood or another county just

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:44.259
because their parents are

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:45.759
dissatisfied with local schools?

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.259
It really comes down to what is your

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.089
vision for the public

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.169
education system?

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:51.549
The school choice argument is

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:52.599
actually the system should be

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.979
responsive to the parents.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.539
They are the ultimate stakeholders.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.189
That's how you preserve political

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.229
support for public education.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.239
I would never send Daniel to the

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.159
district school because I know what

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.719
that's like. I've been there before

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.579
with him. We've experienced what

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.379
the data shows.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.819
Before they relocated to Palm

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.289
Springs, Daniel was enrolled in a

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:12.639
public school in the town of Lake

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.469
Elsinore last year, sued

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:15.999
the school for mistreatment and for

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.349
failing to meet Daniel's learning

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:18.249
needs.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.898
Shortly after the case was settled,

00:04:19.899 --> 00:04:21.518
they moved away because Laster said

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:22.779
she was the victim of domestic

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:23.780
violence.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.719
By the time Daniel was in first

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.669
grade, the teacher mistreated

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.649
him by the second grade.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:35.659
He was emotionally vanquished,

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.579
he had suicidal ideation

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.199
and he didn't want to go to school

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.389
every day. And so I decided

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.359
to immediately pull him

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.219
out of that school

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.139
in that school district and

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.099
homeschool him.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.049
But after probably about

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.939
a year and a half, I

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.889
recognize that that

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.419
can become very expensive.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.669
And one of those years I

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.529
enrolled him in Springs

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.419
Public Charter School

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:03.379
around the same time.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:04.919
Right, Daniel?

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.480
Three hours till

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.779
we were to look at what happens

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.639
with African-American or black

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.859
males in this country,

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.709
if they're able to read and write

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.609
then and if they're excessively

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:18.959
punished, that's what we call the

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.459
school to prison pipeline.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.839
I don't want my son on the school to

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.609
prison pipeline.

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.919
I want him to stay on the path he's

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.539
he's at grade level.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:29.279
He's not building in English

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.600
language arts or math,

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.539
which is huge for fifth grade black

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.459
boys in the state of California.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.199
Despite Daniel's academic progress,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.639
Laster is considering homeschooling

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:40.589
him again to avoid the commute.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.089
The Springs Charter School Network

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.349
offers programs that support

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:44.879
homeschool families and study at

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.829
home education school

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.139
transportation.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:49.649
It's for a lot of people.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:50.699
It's like the plumbing in your

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.439
house. It's not something you think

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.629
about much until it doesn't work.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.579
The pandemic has forced

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.659
that to the fore. Now people are

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.739
paying attention to school

00:05:58.740 --> 00:05:59.939
transportation because of these

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.199
shortages and so forth.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.879
But these are long standing issues

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.619
of a system that just doesn't work

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:05.939
as well as it could, but kind of is

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.199
in the background and people aren't

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.009
thinking about.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:08.939
And some of these issues we're

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.439
seeing now around choice and parents

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:11.789
wanting different things are going

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:12.869
to bring that to the surface.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.579
I especially believe that

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.409
for parents like myself

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.629
that are single parents

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.519
being able to be offered

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.409
a resource to allow their

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.389
kids to get to that quality school

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.699
of, you know, of their choosing

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:29.700
is a must.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.779
Hi everybody.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.759
I am not going to be on camera.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.409
I may be multi-tasking, but I'm

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.410
present in the meeting.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.429
I've done everything that I possibly

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.469
can with them. A day I can become

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:43.580
very overwhelmed.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.499
I want my son to be educated, I want

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.419
my son to have upward mobility, so

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.369
I sacrifice now to

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.169
make sure that he has the best

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.089
outcomes possible later in life.

